Neo Geo SDK · sound/samples/
============================

WAV sample sources for ADPCM-A and ADPCM-B playback on the YM2610.

Layout
------

  in_wav_a/      WAV inputs that will be encoded to ADPCM-A
                 (6 short trigger-and-forget channels, percussion-like)
  in_wav_b/      WAV inputs that will be encoded to ADPCM-B
                 (1 streamed channel, music beds / long voices)

Pipeline
--------

  in_wav_a/*.wav   --enc_wave16le_a-->  ADPCM-A blocks
  in_wav_b/*.wav   --enc_wave16le_b-->  ADPCM-B stream

Both encoders are pure-Python (see sound/tools/) so no native binary is
required.  SoX is optional for WAV resampling but the pipeline runs
without it.

Build
-----

  make samples    # re-encode all WAV inputs
  make vrom       # bundle the V ROM
  make sound      # full audio pipeline

SDK identifiers
---------------

  ADPCM-A trigger samples (sdk/sound_ids.h SOUND_SFX_*):
    COIN_CHIME / START_SLASH / TITLE_GONG / INTRO_TAIKO /
    FOOTSTEP / SHORT_SHOUT / BLADE_WHOOSH / IMPACT_HIT /
    STRING_PHRASE / LOW_DRUM / READY_VOICE / ATTACK_VOICE

  ADPCM-B streamed beds:
    SOUND_BED_TITLE_THEME / STAGE_ONE / STAGE_TWO /
    SOUND_BED_ENDING_THEME / EYECATCHER

See SOURCES.md for the licensing + provenance of each WAV.
